WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.620
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit 5: Outdoor
Adventures and Environmental Protection.

2
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.460
This unit takes you into the great outdoors.

3
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.260
You will explore topics connected to outdoor
adventures, nature and environmental protection.

4
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:21.020
Whether it is hiking through a forest, camping beside a
river, or working together to protect the natural world,

5
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:27.820
this unit gives you the language skills to describe,
discuss and write about these experiences with confidence.

6
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:34.180
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:41.360
By the end of this unit, you will be able to use
vocabulary related to outdoor equipment, adventure sports,

8
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.200
nature features and eco-friendly practices.

9
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:50.180
You will also read and understand texts about
outdoor activities and environmental challenges.

10
00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:59.240
You will also use -ing forms (gerunds and present participles)
correctly as subjects, objects and after prepositions.

11
00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.840
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:10.300
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: discovery,
effectiveness, flexibility, generalisation, greenhouse,

13
00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:11.340
dioxide.

14
00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.980
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:20.660
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:26.100
The reading sequence includes Guardians
of the Green and Eco-Club Field Reports.

17
00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:27.600
Read actively.

18
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.960
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:37.220
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:42.720
The first language focus is -ing
Forms (Gerunds and Participles).

21
00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:47.620
The -ing form of a verb can act as a noun, called a gerund.

22
00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:55.080
In this unit you use gerunds in three places: as the
subject of a sentence, as the object after certain verbs,

23
00:01:55.660 --> 00:02:00.400
and after prepositions — all of which are
common when writing about outdoor activities.

24
00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:08.080
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

25
00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:15.120
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: Describe Your Ideal Outdoor Adventure.

26
00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:20.300
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

27
00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.660
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

28
00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.180
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

29
00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:28.920
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:35.920
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

31
00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.500
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

32
00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:45.880
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
